1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:06,560
I also set out my outfit the night before so that I don't have to think about what to wear in the morning.
我也会在前一天晚上准备好衣服，这样早上就不用再想穿什么。

2
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:10,640
One of the benefits of a routine is that it takes away choice.
固定习惯的一个好处，就是减少需要做的选择。

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:14,000
Genuinely, I find too many choices very overwhelming.
说真的，选择太多会让我觉得难以应付。

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,560
And so I like to eliminate as many choices as I possibly can in the mornings because it helps me stay efficient and focused.
所以我喜欢尽可能减少早晨需要做的选择，因为这样能帮我保持高效和专注。

5
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:26,360
So if you're the same as me, then this is definitely something I would recommend.
所以，如果你也和我一样，这确实是我会推荐的方法。

6
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:37,599
And I like to wait a little bit between putting on that ordinary serum and some SPF face cream because otherwise the texture just goes very strange.
涂过那款精华之后，我喜欢稍等一下再涂防晒面霜，不然质地会变得有点奇怪。

7
00:00:37,599 --> 00:00:41,480
I also put on some caffeine eye cream.
我还会涂一点含咖啡因的眼霜。

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:46,279
Um, and as you can see, my skin is always so red after putting on face cream.
嗯，你也能看到，我涂完面霜之后皮肤总是红红的。

9
00:00:46,279 --> 00:00:48,920
I will also put on some CC cream.
我还会涂一点 CC 霜。

10
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:54,160
I put this on everyday, actually.
其实，我每天都会涂这个。

11
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:55,880
And there's my makeup done.
这样，我的妆就化好了。

12
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:58,600
By this time, my green tea has cooled as well.
这时候，我的绿茶也放凉一些了。

13
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:04,800
I don't, like, have it straight out of the kettle because it's usually just a bit too hot.
我不会刚从水壶里倒出来就喝，因为那时通常还有点太烫。

14
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,200
But then I will sit down at my desk with my tea.
然后，我会端着茶在书桌前坐下来。

15
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,559
And I tried to do some Latin first thing.
接着，我一早先学一点拉丁语。

16
00:01:10,559 --> 00:01:14,520
So today I was doing a translation from John's gospel.
所以今天，我在翻译《约翰福音》中的一段文字。

17
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:21,679
I find this is a great task for the morning because it gets my brain working and gets me thinking, but it's not too intense.
我觉得这很适合早晨做，因为它能让大脑运转起来、开始思考，又不会太吃力。

18
00:01:21,679 --> 00:01:28,800
Plus, I'm trying to practice Latin every day, so this is a great way to make sure that I get some Latin practice in.
另外，我正努力每天练拉丁语，所以这也是确保自己能抽空练习的好办法。

19
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:44,320
And then after doing that I will write my to-do list.
做完这些之后，我会写下待办清单。

20
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:49,549
Of course I use the academic planner from Pumpkin Productivity, which is my stationery shop.
当然，我用的是自己文具店 Pumpkin Productivity 出的学业计划本。

21
00:01:49,559 --> 00:01:52,959
I design this planner and so of course I'm going to use it every day.
这个计划本是我设计的，所以我当然每天都会用它。

22
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:57,679
I just pop in my key events from my calendar and then write a to-do list.
我把日历里的重要安排填进去，然后再写待办清单。

23
00:01:57,679 --> 00:02:01,880
By this time, it's also usually light, so I'll open up my curtains.
这时天通常也亮了，所以我会拉开窗帘。

24
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:10,080
And I didn't show this before, but I always open my window as soon as I wake up so that my room's less stuffy.
前面没拍到，不过我总是一醒来就开窗，让房间不那么闷。

25
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,669
Next, it's time for breakfast.
接下来，该吃早餐了。

26
00:02:11,679 --> 00:02:14,279
Breakfast is my favorite meal of the day, honestly.
说真的，早餐是我一天里最喜欢的一餐。

27
00:02:14,279 --> 00:02:15,800
So I have one of two things.
所以，我通常会在两种早餐里选一种。

28
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:19,720
I either will have yogurt in my room or I'll go and make some porridge.
我要么在房间里吃酸奶，要么去煮点燕麦粥。

29
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:25,000
But on days that I have 9:00 a.m. classes, I tend to just have yogurt because it's very quick.
不过，有早上九点的课时，我一般就吃酸奶，因为很省时间。

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,119
I know it doesn't look that appetizing, but it's really tasty.
我知道它看起来没那么诱人，但其实很好吃。

31
00:02:29,119 --> 00:02:32,320
After breakfast, I will get back to doing a little bit more work.
吃过早餐，我会继续做一点事情。

32
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:43,520
This time it would just be anything from my to-do list though, so today I was working on an essay.
不过，这次就是做待办清单里的事情了；今天我在写一篇论文。

33
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:47,040
And then I try to spend at least 5 minutes writing.
然后，我会试着至少花五分钟写点东西。

34
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:49,829
So this might be journaling, this might be writing a poem.
可能是写日记，也可能是写一首诗。

35
00:02:49,839 --> 00:02:55,200
Sometimes I'll leave my room to do this, and I do prefer to do this out of my room, actually outside or in a cafe.
有时我会离开房间去写；我确实更喜欢在房间外，比如户外或咖啡馆里写。

36
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:59,360
But on days that I have 9:00 a.m. classes, I would just spend 5 minutes doing this in my room, room.
但有早上九点的课时，我就只在房间里花五分钟写一写。

37
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,200
So I wrote a very terrible poem this morning.
所以今天早上，我写了一首很糟糕的诗。
